From ca785e136c57772782abc194bd630a2c96af2c10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:53:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 056/118] tools decode-link: forms of links found in the wild

Checked against 257 example links of panels, clients and public lists:
- parameter names in any case, other spellings of the insecure flag, the
  server name and the packet encoding, the "amp;" of links copied from HTML;
- a Trojan password with "/";
- XHTTP settings written as parameters of the link next to or instead of
  "extra", the mode as v2rayA names it, "extra" escaped twice;
- whole numbers written with a fraction in ranges;
- the name of the WebSocket early data header;
- a warning for every parameter that is not read, and for unknown keys of
  "xmux".
